WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.350
Test week is coming: eight tests.

2
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:07.120
Some of you take two or three of them, so

3
00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:09.080
those tests can’t be at the same time.

4
00:00:09.750 --> 00:00:11.110
How few times do we need?

5
00:00:12.410 --> 00:00:14.830
Today: share out times with no

6
00:00:14.830 --> 00:00:17.430
clashes, and fair turns for everyone.

7
00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:20.760
Draw each test as a dot.

8
00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:23.980
Join two dots with a line when

9
00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:26.060
one pupil takes both tests.

10
00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:29.340
A line means: not at the same time!

11
00:00:30.550 --> 00:00:32.610
Now give each dot a colour:

12
00:00:33.310 --> 00:00:34.790
each colour is a time.

13
00:00:35.460 --> 00:00:38.140
Two dots joined by a line must

14
00:00:38.140 --> 00:00:39.360
get different colours.

15
00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:42.460
Use as few colours as you can.

16
00:00:43.740 --> 00:00:47.260
Omar takes maths, Arabic and French.

17
00:00:48.020 --> 00:00:50.500
All three are joined to each other, so

18
00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:52.180
they need three different times.

19
00:00:52.870 --> 00:00:55.870
So three times is the fewest we can use.

20
00:00:57.150 --> 00:00:57.630
Quick check!

21
00:00:58.240 --> 00:01:01.220
Maths and art are not joined by a line.

22
00:01:01.890 --> 00:01:03.350
Can they be at the same time?

23
00:01:04.660 --> 00:01:07.400
Yes: no line means no clash.

24
00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:10.060
Sharing a time saves a slot.

25
00:01:10.790 --> 00:01:13.250
Going down the list in order needs four

26
00:01:13.250 --> 00:01:15.750
times, but a clever order needs only

27
00:01:15.750 --> 00:01:16.030
three.

28
00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:18.540
Here’s the clever trick:

29
00:01:18.980 --> 00:01:20.820
colour the hardest dot next.

30
00:01:21.530 --> 00:01:22.950
That’s the one whose neighbours

31
00:01:22.950 --> 00:01:24.630
already use the most colours.

32
00:01:25.410 --> 00:01:28.110
Computers plan real exam weeks like this.

33
00:01:29.340 --> 00:01:32.360
Times can be fair or unfair too.

34
00:01:32.970 --> 00:01:35.410
If one pupil gets three tests in one

35
00:01:35.410 --> 00:01:38.510
morning and another gets one, that’s not

36
00:01:38.510 --> 00:01:38.790
fair.

37
00:01:39.520 --> 00:01:41.280
A good plan spreads each

38
00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:42.480
pupil’s tests out.

39
00:01:43.730 --> 00:01:46.090
It’s the same with turns: who goes

40
00:01:46.090 --> 00:01:48.130
first in a game, who cleans the

41
00:01:48.130 --> 00:01:49.990
board, who sits by the window.

42
00:01:50.670 --> 00:01:52.850
Take turns, so nobody always

43
00:01:52.850 --> 00:01:53.990
gets the worst one.

44
00:01:55.180 --> 00:01:57.700
In the app, tap the tests to give

45
00:01:57.700 --> 00:01:59.680
them times, with no red lines.

46
00:02:00.370 --> 00:02:02.770
Then press Greedy, and DSatur.

47
00:02:03.460 --> 00:02:05.380
How few times are really enough?

48
00:02:06.690 --> 00:02:07.230
Your turn.

49
00:02:07.840 --> 00:02:09.680
Omar’s three tests all

50
00:02:09.680 --> 00:02:10.840
clash with each other.

51
00:02:11.470 --> 00:02:13.070
Can two times be enough

52
00:02:13.070 --> 00:02:13.990
for the whole week?

53
00:02:15.310 --> 00:02:17.470
No: three tests that all

54
00:02:17.470 --> 00:02:19.570
clash need three times.

55
00:02:20.250 --> 00:02:22.670
Remember: a line means not

56
00:02:22.670 --> 00:02:23.710
at the same time.

57
00:02:24.340 --> 00:02:25.940
Colour the hardest first.

58
00:02:26.770 --> 00:02:28.630
And spread out turns fairly.

59
00:02:29.950 --> 00:02:32.350
Try it at school: draw your class’s

60
00:02:32.350 --> 00:02:35.170
clubs or games as dots, and join the

61
00:02:35.170 --> 00:02:36.690
ones a friend does both of.

62
00:02:37.290 --> 00:02:38.810
Colour them with as few

63
00:02:38.810 --> 00:02:39.910
colours as you can.

64
00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:42.820
Then make a fair rota for a class

65
00:02:42.820 --> 00:02:45.080
job, so everyone takes a turn.
